    execution surfaces: lane R — the raw root + the one SQL implementation as a fourth column of the lane matrix
    
    Pass 3 made the shared SQL path (deals_raw / labels_raw → deals_landed_v1 → new_deals_batch_rows → new_deals_batch) what every
    lane executes; the matrix still showed it as text inside the A and C cells, so "the parallel lane" read as three code paths that
    must agree after it had become one.
    
    - docs/execution_surfaces.yaml: surfaces.R; an R cell in each of the 18 layers and 13 pipeline steps (how the layer is performed
      inside BigQuery, or why it is n/a: no runtime, trigger, secret, delivery or write-back of its own); L6 flips to Parallel (one
      duplicate rule for every lane, D3); the legend names the fourth column as the implementation, not a scenario. Workbook rebuilt
      (verify OK: Layers 5/3/10, steps 2/5/6).
    - docs/architecture.yaml: scenario R declared; the shared blocks tagged R (the two SQL files, land_raw.sql, backfill_raw.sh, the
      DDL, the UDF, the pass-3 tests and page); sql/refresh_pipeline_labels.sh re-layered to L4 (it extracts labels). Tree regenerated
      (this commit also restores the renders that 2df5822 generated with an untracked file on disk).
    - docs/EXECUTION_SURFACES.md: a lane row and a timeline row; docs/SCENARIOS.md §R; README "Read in this order" item 3; the PASS3
      page names the lane.
    
